{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01MTbExgW5WnaXju2rbX1q9r","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! Now I have enough information to provide a comprehensive summary. Let me compile the findings:\n\n## Tank Simulation Startup Configuration Flow - Comprehensive Report\n\nBased on my thorough analysis of the codebase, here's the complete picture of what's currently configurable at startup versus what's hardcoded/defaulted:\n\n---\n\n### 1. TUI Startup Flow (crates/tank_tui/src/main.rs)\n\n**Startup Configuration Selection:**\n- Interactive three-field selection screen with keyboard navigation (arrows, Enter)\n- Defaults: Scenario index 0 (nano_cycle), Size index 1 (Baseline 1.0x), Fill index 1 (90%)\n- Navigation: Up/Down move between fields, Left/Right adjust values, Enter confirms\n\n**Selection Fields:**\n1. **Scenario** - Selects from `tank_scenarios::default_scenario_ids()` (3 scenarios)\n2. **Tank Size** - Preset scale multipliers\n3. **Fill Height** - Ratio applied to fill_height_cm\n4. **Launch** - Final confirmation\n\n**Post-Selection Processing:**\n```\n1. Load scenario preset by ID\n2. Create ScenarioGeometryOverrides with size_scale and fill_ratio\n3. Generate random seed from system clock (Unix timestamp)\n4. Call seeded_state_with_overrides() to materialize state\n5. Initialize TuiApp with Engine, save path, and formatted scenario label\n```\n\n---\n\n### 2. Scenario Model (crates/tank_data/src/presets.rs, line 750)\n\n**ScenarioPreset Structure:**\n```rust\npub struct ScenarioPreset {\n    pub id: String,                      // e.g., \"nano_cycle\"\n    pub name: String,                    // e.g., \"Nano Cycle\"\n    pub source_water_id: String,         // Water profile ID\n    pub substrate_ids: Vec<String>,      // Substrate layer references\n    pub plant_ids: Vec<String>,          // Plant guild references\n    pub shrimp_profile_id: String,       // Shrimp species preset\n    pub process_params_id: String,       // Chemistry/process parameters\n    pub tank_length_cm: f64,             // Base geometry\n    pub tank_width_cm: f64,\n    pub tank_height_cm: f64,\n    pub fill_height_cm: f64,\n    pub ambient_temp_c: f64,             // Initial ambient temperature\n    pub provenance: Option<Provenance>,  // Metadata\n}\n```\n\n**Available Scenarios (3 total):**\n\n| Scenario | ID | Tank (cm) | Fill (cm) | Ambient | Source Water | Substrates | Plants |\n|----------|----|----|----|----|---|---|---|\n| Nano Cycle | nano_cycle | 30×20×20 | 18 | 24°C | soft_acidic | inert_sand | fast_stem |\n| Medium Planted | medium_planted | 60×30×36 | 32 | 24°C | moderate | active_planted, coarse_porous | fast_stem, root_rosette |\n| Warm Room | warm_room | 45×24×28 | 24 | 29°C | moderate | inert_gravel | fast_stem |\n\n---\n\n### 3. Scenario Materialization (crates/tank_scenarios/src/lib.rs, lines 172-310)\n\n**Geometry Overrides Applied:**\n```\ntank.length_cm *= size_scale\ntank.width_cm *= size_scale\ntank.height_cm *= size_scale\nfill_height_cm = (fill_height_cm * size_scale * fill_ratio).min(tank_height_cm)\n```\n\n**Materialization Process (seeded_state):**\n1. **Geometry** - From scenario + overrides, with hardcoded glass_thickness_mm: 5.0, open_top: true, lid_exchange_factor: 0.25\n2. **Initial Water State** - Populated from source-water profile × fill volume (WaterState::from_source_profile)\n3. **Source-Water Catalog** - All known presets loaded: soft_acidic, moderate, hard_shrimp, ro_like\n4. **Process Parameters** - From scenario's process_params_id (currently only \"default\" exists)\n5. **Substrate Layers** - Loaded from preset files, footprint calculated from geometry\n6. **Plant Guilds** - Loaded from preset files with initialization:\n   - biomass_g: 5.0 (hardcoded)\n   - health_index: 0.8 (hardcoded)\n   - crowding_index: 0.1 (hardcoded)\n   - habitat_index: depends on substrate CEC or 0.8 for FastStem\n7. **Shrimp Parameters** - From loaded shrimp preset\n8. **Hardware** - ALL DEFAULTS (see section 4 below)\n9. **Microbes, Filter, Algae, Animals, Detritus** - ALL DEFAULTS\n\n---\n\n### 4. HeaterState::default() (crates/tank_core/src/types/hardware.rs, lines 60-71)\n\n**Default Hardware State - ALL HARDCODED AND NOT CONFIGURABLE AT STARTUP:**\n\n```rust\nimpl Default for HeaterState {\n    fn default() -> Self {\n        Self {\n            enabled: false,              // Heater OFF by default\n            setpoint_c: 24.0,            // Hardcoded\n            deadband_c: 0.5,             // Hardcoded\n            max_watts: 50.0,             // Hardcoded\n            efficiency: 1.0,             // Hardcoded (perfect)\n            last_output_w: 0.0,\n        }\n    }\n}\n```\n\n**Other Hardware Defaults:**\n\n| Component | Field | Default | Hardcoded |\n|-----------|-------|---------|-----------|\n| **Light** | enabled | true | Yes |\n| | photoperiod_hours | 8.0 | Yes |\n| | intensity_index | 0.7 | Yes |\n| **Filter** | enabled | true | Yes |\n| | flow_lph | 200.0 | Yes |\n| | cleanliness_index | 1.0 (pristine) | Yes |\n| **Aeration** | enabled | false | Yes |\n| | intensity | 0.0 | Yes |\n| **FilterState** | biofilter_maturity_index | 0.1 (immature) | Yes |\n| | clogging_index | 0.0 | Yes |\n| | seeded_biomass_index | 0.0 (unseeded) | Yes |\n\n**Key Finding:** The only scenario that overrides default hardware is the internal `cycling_base_state()` fixture, which enables aeration at 0.3 intensity.\n\n---\n\n### 5. PlayerAction Variants & Actions Screen (crates/tank_core/src/types/actions.rs + crates/tank_tui/src/screens/actions.rs)\n\n**12 Available PlayerAction Variants:**\n\n```rust\nenum PlayerAction {\n    Feed { grams: f64 },\n    WaterChangePercent { percent: f64, source_profile_id: String },\n    TrimPlants { fraction: f64 },\n    SiphonDetritus { fraction: f64 },\n    CleanFilter { intensity: f64 },\n    AddShrimp { count: u32 },\n    RemoveShrimp { count: u32 },\n    ChangePhotoperiod { hours: f64 },           // Changes light duration\n    ChangeLightIntensity { intensity_index: f64 }, // Changes light brightness\n    ChangeHeaterSetpoint { setpoint_c: f64 },  // Changes heater target temp\n    ChangeAmbientTemperature { target_c: f64 }, // Changes room temp\n    ChangeAeration { enabled: bool, intensity: f64 },\n}\n```\n\n**Actions Screen Structure (crates/tank_tui/src/screens/actions.rs):**\n\n- **Left Panel:** List of 12 action variants (cyan highlight on selected)\n- **Right Panel (Top):** Form for selected action with 1-2 fields per action\n- **Right Panel (Bottom):** Help text\n\n**ActionFormState Default Values:**\n\n| Action | Field | Default | Type |\n|--------|-------|---------|------|\n| Feed | grams | 0.20 | f64 |\n| Water Change | percent | 25.0 | f64 |\n| | source | index 1 (moderate) | choice |\n| Trim Plants | fraction | 0.25 | f64 0.0-1.0 |\n| Siphon Detritus | fraction | 0.30 | f64 0.0-1.0 |\n| Clean Filter | intensity | 0.50 | f64 0.0-1.0 |\n| Add Shrimp | count | 5 | u32 |\n| Remove Shrimp | count | 2 | u32 |\n| Photoperiod | hours | 8.0 | f64 0.0-24.0 |\n| Light Intensity | intensity | 0.70 | f64 0.0-1.0 |\n| Heater Setpoint | setpoint_c | 24.0 | f64 > 0 |\n| Ambient Temp | target_c | 24.0 | f64 > 0 |\n| Aeration | enabled | true | boolean |\n| | intensity | 0.40 | f64 0.0-1.0 |\n\n**Field Types:**\n- Numeric (float) - Most fields, allow digits and '.'\n- Numeric (integer) - Shrimp counts only\n- Choice - Water change source (cycles through 4 source water presets via [ / ])\n- Toggle - Aeration enabled (toggle via 't')\n\n---\n\n### 6. Preset Data in crates/tank_data\n\n**Available Preset Categories:**\n\n| Category | IDs | Notes |\n|----------|-----|-------|\n| **Source Water** | soft_acidic, moderate, hard_shrimp, ro_like | 4 profiles with chemistry parameters |\n| **Substrates** | inert_sand, inert_gravel, active_planted, coarse_porous | 4 types with nutrient capacity |\n| **Plants** | fast_stem, root_rosette | 2 guilds (growth rates, nutrient uptake) |\n| **Shrimp** | neocaridina_davidi | 1 species (only option) |\n| **Process Params** | default | 1 set (only option) |\n| **Scenarios** | nano_cycle, medium_planted, warm_room | 3 presets |\n| **Filters** | ❌ NONE | No preset filter hardware configs |\n| **Lights** | ❌ NONE | No preset light hardware configs |\n| **Heaters** | ❌ NONE | No preset heater hardware configs |\n| **Aeration** | ❌ NONE | No preset aeration hardware configs |\n\n---\n\n### SUMMARY: What's Configurable vs. Hardcoded at Startup\n\n**CONFIGURABLE AT STARTUP:**\n1. ✅ Scenario selection (3 options)\n2. ✅ Tank size scale (0.8x, 1.0x, 1.25x multiplier)\n3. ✅ Fill height ratio (75%, 90%, 100%)\n4. ✅ Random seed (from clock, non-interactive)\n\n**HARDCODED/DEFAULTED AT STARTUP:**\n1. ❌ All hardware (light, heater, filter, aeration)\n   - Light: ON, 8h photoperiod, 0.7 intensity\n   - Heater: OFF, 24°C setpoint, 50W max, 0.5°C deadband\n   - Filter: ON, 200 LPH, pristine condition\n   - Aeration: OFF, 0.0 intensity\n   - Filter state: Immature (0.1 index), unseeded (0 index), unclogged\n2. ❌ All hardware can only be changed POST-STARTUP via Actions screen\n3. ❌ Initial microbe biomass (defaults to zero)\n4. ❌ Initial filter maturity (0.1 - immature)\n5. ❌ Initial plant biomass (5.0g) and health (0.8 index)\n6. ❌ Shrimp species (only neocaridina_davidi available)\n7. ❌ Process parameters (only \"default\" available)\n8. ❌ Substrate depth and composition (fixed per scenario)\n9. ❌ Tank glass thickness (5.0mm) and open-top design\n\n**Where Hardware Can Be Modified:**\n- All hardware parameters can be changed at ANY time during simulation via the Actions screen\n- Light: photoperiod (0-24h) and intensity (0-1.0) via ChangePhotoperiod and ChangeLightIntensity actions\n- Heater: setpoint temperature via ChangeHeaterSetpoint action\n- Aeration: enable/disable and intensity (0-1.0) via ChangeAeration action\n- Filter: indirect via CleanFilter action (reduces clogging_index)\n- Ambient temperature: via ChangeAmbientTemperature action\n\n---\n\n**File Locations Summary:**\n- Main startup: `/root/tank-simulation/crates/tank_tui/src/main.rs` (lines 38-224)\n- Scenario model: `/root/tank-simulation/crates/tank_data/src/presets.rs` (line 750)\n- Materialization: `/root/tank-simulation/crates/tank_scenarios/src/lib.rs` (lines 172-310)\n- Hardware defaults: `/root/tank-simulation/crates/tank_core/src/types/hardware.rs` (lines 50-101)\n- Actions interface: `/root/tank-simulation/crates/tank_tui/src/screens/actions.rs` (lines 1-480)\n- Tank size/fill presets: `/root/tank-simulation/crates/tank_tui/src/lib.rs` (lines 90-118)"},{"type":"text","text":"agentId: a5f32c96421869b7a (for resuming to continue this agent's work if needed)\n<usage>total_tokens: 55888\ntool_uses: 22\nduration_ms: 54609</usage>"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"52ade16c-d21b-4a80-87c4-793dd732d7a8","uuid":"5c4eadeb-ac83-447d-8ad9-9a215c262a4f","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"I need to understand the current startup configuration flow for this tank simulation project. Specifically:\n\n1. How does the TUI main.rs handle startup/scenario selection? Look at crates/tank_tui/src/main.rs\n2. What does the scenario model look like in crates/tank_data/src/presets.rs (around line 750)?\n3. How does scenario materialization work in crates/tank_scenarios/src/lib.rs (around lines 172 and 295)?\n4. What does HeaterState::default() look like in crates/tank_core/src/types/hardware.rs?\n5. What are the current PlayerAction variants and how is the actions screen structured in crates/tank_tui/src/screens/actions.rs?\n6. What filter/light/heater preset data exists in crates/tank_data?\n\nBe thorough - read relevant sections of all these files and report back with the key details about what's currently configurable at startup vs what's hardcoded/defaulted.","agentId":"a5f32c96421869b7a","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! Now I have enough information to provide a comprehensive summary. Let me compile the findings:\n\n## Tank Simulation Startup Configuration Flow - Comprehensive Report\n\nBased on my thorough analysis of the codebase, here's the complete picture of what's currently configurable at startup versus what's hardcoded/defaulted:\n\n---\n\n### 1. TUI Startup Flow (crates/tank_tui/src/main.rs)\n\n**Startup Configuration Selection:**\n- Interactive three-field selection screen with keyboard navigation (arrows, Enter)\n- Defaults: Scenario index 0 (nano_cycle), Size index 1 (Baseline 1.0x), Fill index 1 (90%)\n- Navigation: Up/Down move between fields, Left/Right adjust values, Enter confirms\n\n**Selection Fields:**\n1. **Scenario** - Selects from `tank_scenarios::default_scenario_ids()` (3 scenarios)\n2. **Tank Size** - Preset scale multipliers\n3. **Fill Height** - Ratio applied to fill_height_cm\n4. **Launch** - Final confirmation\n\n**Post-Selection Processing:**\n```\n1. Load scenario preset by ID\n2. Create ScenarioGeometryOverrides with size_scale and fill_ratio\n3. Generate random seed from system clock (Unix timestamp)\n4. Call seeded_state_with_overrides() to materialize state\n5. Initialize TuiApp with Engine, save path, and formatted scenario label\n```\n\n---\n\n### 2. Scenario Model (crates/tank_data/src/presets.rs, line 750)\n\n**ScenarioPreset Structure:**\n```rust\npub struct ScenarioPreset {\n    pub id: String,                      // e.g., \"nano_cycle\"\n    pub name: String,                    // e.g., \"Nano Cycle\"\n    pub source_water_id: String,         // Water profile ID\n    pub substrate_ids: Vec<String>,      // Substrate layer references\n    pub plant_ids: Vec<String>,          // Plant guild references\n    pub shrimp_profile_id: String,       // Shrimp species preset\n    pub process_params_id: String,       // Chemistry/process parameters\n    pub tank_length_cm: f64,             // Base geometry\n    pub tank_width_cm: f64,\n    pub tank_height_cm: f64,\n    pub fill_height_cm: f64,\n    pub ambient_temp_c: f64,             // Initial ambient temperature\n    pub provenance: Option<Provenance>,  // Metadata\n}\n```\n\n**Available Scenarios (3 total):**\n\n| Scenario | ID | Tank (cm) | Fill (cm) | Ambient | Source Water | Substrates | Plants |\n|----------|----|----|----|----|---|---|---|\n| Nano Cycle | nano_cycle | 30×20×20 | 18 | 24°C | soft_acidic | inert_sand | fast_stem |\n| Medium Planted | medium_planted | 60×30×36 | 32 | 24°C | moderate | active_planted, coarse_porous | fast_stem, root_rosette |\n| Warm Room | warm_room | 45×24×28 | 24 | 29°C | moderate | inert_gravel | fast_stem |\n\n---\n\n### 3. Scenario Materialization (crates/tank_scenarios/src/lib.rs, lines 172-310)\n\n**Geometry Overrides Applied:**\n```\ntank.length_cm *= size_scale\ntank.width_cm *= size_scale\ntank.height_cm *= size_scale\nfill_height_cm = (fill_height_cm * size_scale * fill_ratio).min(tank_height_cm)\n```\n\n**Materialization Process (seeded_state):**\n1. **Geometry** - From scenario + overrides, with hardcoded glass_thickness_mm: 5.0, open_top: true, lid_exchange_factor: 0.25\n2. **Initial Water State** - Populated from source-water profile × fill volume (WaterState::from_source_profile)\n3. **Source-Water Catalog** - All known presets loaded: soft_acidic, moderate, hard_shrimp, ro_like\n4. **Process Parameters** - From scenario's process_params_id (currently only \"default\" exists)\n5. **Substrate Layers** - Loaded from preset files, footprint calculated from geometry\n6. **Plant Guilds** - Loaded from preset files with initialization:\n   - biomass_g: 5.0 (hardcoded)\n   - health_index: 0.8 (hardcoded)\n   - crowding_index: 0.1 (hardcoded)\n   - habitat_index: depends on substrate CEC or 0.8 for FastStem\n7. **Shrimp Parameters** - From loaded shrimp preset\n8. **Hardware** - ALL DEFAULTS (see section 4 below)\n9. **Microbes, Filter, Algae, Animals, Detritus** - ALL DEFAULTS\n\n---\n\n### 4. HeaterState::default() (crates/tank_core/src/types/hardware.rs, lines 60-71)\n\n**Default Hardware State - ALL HARDCODED AND NOT CONFIGURABLE AT STARTUP:**\n\n```rust\nimpl Default for HeaterState {\n    fn default() -> Self {\n        Self {\n            enabled: false,              // Heater OFF by default\n            setpoint_c: 24.0,            // Hardcoded\n            deadband_c: 0.5,             // Hardcoded\n            max_watts: 50.0,             // Hardcoded\n            efficiency: 1.0,             // Hardcoded (perfect)\n            last_output_w: 0.0,\n        }\n    }\n}\n```\n\n**Other Hardware Defaults:**\n\n| Component | Field | Default | Hardcoded |\n|-----------|-------|---------|-----------|\n| **Light** | enabled | true | Yes |\n| | photoperiod_hours | 8.0 | Yes |\n| | intensity_index | 0.7 | Yes |\n| **Filter** | enabled | true | Yes |\n| | flow_lph | 200.0 | Yes |\n| | cleanliness_index | 1.0 (pristine) | Yes |\n| **Aeration** | enabled | false | Yes |\n| | intensity | 0.0 | Yes |\n| **FilterState** | biofilter_maturity_index | 0.1 (immature) | Yes |\n| | clogging_index | 0.0 | Yes |\n| | seeded_biomass_index | 0.0 (unseeded) | Yes |\n\n**Key Finding:** The only scenario that overrides default hardware is the internal `cycling_base_state()` fixture, which enables aeration at 0.3 intensity.\n\n---\n\n### 5. PlayerAction Variants & Actions Screen (crates/tank_core/src/types/actions.rs + crates/tank_tui/src/screens/actions.rs)\n\n**12 Available PlayerAction Variants:**\n\n```rust\nenum PlayerAction {\n    Feed { grams: f64 },\n    WaterChangePercent { percent: f64, source_profile_id: String },\n    TrimPlants { fraction: f64 },\n    SiphonDetritus { fraction: f64 },\n    CleanFilter { intensity: f64 },\n    AddShrimp { count: u32 },\n    RemoveShrimp { count: u32 },\n    ChangePhotoperiod { hours: f64 },           // Changes light duration\n    ChangeLightIntensity { intensity_index: f64 }, // Changes light brightness\n    ChangeHeaterSetpoint { setpoint_c: f64 },  // Changes heater target temp\n    ChangeAmbientTemperature { target_c: f64 }, // Changes room temp\n    ChangeAeration { enabled: bool, intensity: f64 },\n}\n```\n\n**Actions Screen Structure (crates/tank_tui/src/screens/actions.rs):**\n\n- **Left Panel:** List of 12 action variants (cyan highlight on selected)\n- **Right Panel (Top):** Form for selected action with 1-2 fields per action\n- **Right Panel (Bottom):** Help text\n\n**ActionFormState Default Values:**\n\n| Action | Field | Default | Type |\n|--------|-------|---------|------|\n| Feed | grams | 0.20 | f64 |\n| Water Change | percent | 25.0 | f64 |\n| | source | index 1 (moderate) | choice |\n| Trim Plants | fraction | 0.25 | f64 0.0-1.0 |\n| Siphon Detritus | fraction | 0.30 | f64 0.0-1.0 |\n| Clean Filter | intensity | 0.50 | f64 0.0-1.0 |\n| Add Shrimp | count | 5 | u32 |\n| Remove Shrimp | count | 2 | u32 |\n| Photoperiod | hours | 8.0 | f64 0.0-24.0 |\n| Light Intensity | intensity | 0.70 | f64 0.0-1.0 |\n| Heater Setpoint | setpoint_c | 24.0 | f64 > 0 |\n| Ambient Temp | target_c | 24.0 | f64 > 0 |\n| Aeration | enabled | true | boolean |\n| | intensity | 0.40 | f64 0.0-1.0 |\n\n**Field Types:**\n- Numeric (float) - Most fields, allow digits and '.'\n- Numeric (integer) - Shrimp counts only\n- Choice - Water change source (cycles through 4 source water presets via [ / ])\n- Toggle - Aeration enabled (toggle via 't')\n\n---\n\n### 6. Preset Data in crates/tank_data\n\n**Available Preset Categories:**\n\n| Category | IDs | Notes |\n|----------|-----|-------|\n| **Source Water** | soft_acidic, moderate, hard_shrimp, ro_like | 4 profiles with chemistry parameters |\n| **Substrates** | inert_sand, inert_gravel, active_planted, coarse_porous | 4 types with nutrient capacity |\n| **Plants** | fast_stem, root_rosette | 2 guilds (growth rates, nutrient uptake) |\n| **Shrimp** | neocaridina_davidi | 1 species (only option) |\n| **Process Params** | default | 1 set (only option) |\n| **Scenarios** | nano_cycle, medium_planted, warm_room | 3 presets |\n| **Filters** | ❌ NONE | No preset filter hardware configs |\n| **Lights** | ❌ NONE | No preset light hardware configs |\n| **Heaters** | ❌ NONE | No preset heater hardware configs |\n| **Aeration** | ❌ NONE | No preset aeration hardware configs |\n\n---\n\n### SUMMARY: What's Configurable vs. Hardcoded at Startup\n\n**CONFIGURABLE AT STARTUP:**\n1. ✅ Scenario selection (3 options)\n2. ✅ Tank size scale (0.8x, 1.0x, 1.25x multiplier)\n3. ✅ Fill height ratio (75%, 90%, 100%)\n4. ✅ Random seed (from clock, non-interactive)\n\n**HARDCODED/DEFAULTED AT STARTUP:**\n1. ❌ All hardware (light, heater, filter, aeration)\n   - Light: ON, 8h photoperiod, 0.7 intensity\n   - Heater: OFF, 24°C setpoint, 50W max, 0.5°C deadband\n   - Filter: ON, 200 LPH, pristine condition\n   - Aeration: OFF, 0.0 intensity\n   - Filter state: Immature (0.1 index), unseeded (0 index), unclogged\n2. ❌ All hardware can only be changed POST-STARTUP via Actions screen\n3. ❌ Initial microbe biomass (defaults to zero)\n4. ❌ Initial filter maturity (0.1 - immature)\n5. ❌ Initial plant biomass (5.0g) and health (0.8 index)\n6. ❌ Shrimp species (only neocaridina_davidi available)\n7. ❌ Process parameters (only \"default\" available)\n8. ❌ Substrate depth and composition (fixed per scenario)\n9. ❌ Tank glass thickness (5.0mm) and open-top design\n\n**Where Hardware Can Be Modified:**\n- All hardware parameters can be changed at ANY time during simulation via the Actions screen\n- Light: photoperiod (0-24h) and intensity (0-1.0) via ChangePhotoperiod and ChangeLightIntensity actions\n- Heater: setpoint temperature via ChangeHeaterSetpoint action\n- Aeration: enable/disable and intensity (0-1.0) via ChangeAeration action\n- Filter: indirect via CleanFilter action (reduces clogging_index)\n- Ambient temperature: via ChangeAmbientTemperature action\n\n---\n\n**File Locations Summary:**\n- Main startup: `/root/tank-simulation/crates/tank_tui/src/main.rs` (lines 38-224)\n- Scenario model: `/root/tank-simulation/crates/tank_data/src/presets.rs` (line 750)\n- Materialization: `/root/tank-simulation/crates/tank_scenarios/src/lib.rs` (lines 172-310)\n- Hardware defaults: `/root/tank-simulation/crates/tank_core/src/types/hardware.rs` (lines 50-101)\n- Actions interface: `/root/tank-simulation/crates/tank_tui/src/screens/actions.rs` (lines 1-480)\n- Tank size/fill presets: `/root/tank-simulation/crates/tank_tui/src/lib.rs` (lines 90-118)"}],"totalDurationMs":54609,"totalTokens":55888,"totalToolUseCount":22,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2071,"cache_read_input_tokens":50352,"output_tokens":3465,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2071},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01B2c57yExmG4NMdjrBjjjZf","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have a comprehensive understanding of the current state. The completion feedback from the Codex reviewer identified two key gaps:\n\n1. Users can't independently choose substrate, source water, plants, filter, light, heater, and shrimp count at startup - everything is bundled into scenario presets\n2. Heater can't be enabled at startup, shrimp count defaults to zero\n\nThe prompt requirement states:\n> The MVP must allow a user to:\n> - choose a tank size and fill height\n> - choose substrate, source water, plants, filter, light, heater, and shrimp count\n\nSo the next feature should be an enhanced startup configuration screen that lets users independently select each component rather than relying on bundled scenarios.\n\n\nLooking at the available actions, I notice the heater only has a `ChangeHeaterSetpoint` action to modify temperature, but there's no explicit enable/disable action in the PlayerAction spec. Since the prompt requires users to choose the heater at startup, I'll need to figure out how to make the heater configurable during initial setup.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4058,"cache_read_input_tokens":25499,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4058},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"52ade16c-d21b-4a80-87c4-793dd732d7a8","uuid":"ced792d1-741f-4854-9c31-01853ec752f4"}
