{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_011PYLYu2TruP7DdYkZCU2qb","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I now have full context on the gap. Here's the spec:\n\n# Feature: Startup Equipment and Stocking Configuration\n\n## Description\nThe prompt requires that \"the MVP must allow a user to choose substrate, source water, plants, filter, light, heater, and shrimp count.\" Currently, the TUI startup screen only exposes Scenario, Tank Size, and Fill Height — all other choices (source water, substrate, plants, hardware, shrimp) are bundled into the 3 scenario presets with hardcoded defaults for hardware and zero initial shrimp. This feature adds per-component selection fields to the startup configuration screen, extends the scenario materialization path to apply hardware and stocking overrides, and ensures heater-enabled tanks and non-zero initial shrimp populations are achievable from first launch.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] The startup configuration screen includes independently selectable fields for: source water profile, substrate preset, plant selection, filter on/off, light photoperiod, heater enabled + setpoint, aeration on/off, and initial shrimp count\n- [ ] Source water field cycles through all 4 available profiles (`soft_acidic`, `moderate`, `hard_shrimp`, `ro_like`) independently of the scenario\n- [ ] Substrate field cycles through at least 4 preset combinations: `inert_sand`, `inert_gravel`, `active_planted`, `active_planted + coarse_porous` (two-layer)\n- [ ] Plant selection field allows choosing: `FastStem only`, `RootFeedingRosette only`, `Both guilds`, or `None`\n- [ ] Filter field toggles enabled/disabled (defaults to enabled)\n- [ ] Light field cycles through photoperiod presets (e.g., `6h`, `8h`, `10h`, `12h`)\n- [ ] Heater field cycles through options: `Off`, `24°C`, `25°C`, `26°C` (enabled with given setpoint)\n- [ ] Aeration field toggles enabled/disabled (defaults to disabled)\n- [ ] Initial shrimp count field allows setting 0, 5, 10, 15, or 20 shrimp\n- [ ] Scenario field is retained but acts as a template — selecting a scenario sets default values for the new fields, which the user can then override\n- [ ] When a scenario is changed, the override fields reset to that scenario's defaults\n- [ ] The materialization path applies the user's hardware and stocking choices to the `TankState` after scenario materialization\n- [ ] A tank launched with heater enabled starts with `HeaterState.enabled = true` and the selected setpoint\n- [ ] A tank launched with initial shrimp count > 0 starts with that many adults in the `AnimalState`\n- [ ] The startup summary panel updates to reflect the user's current selections (not just the scenario defaults)\n- [ ] All existing acceptance tests continue to pass (they use programmatic scenario materialization, not the TUI startup path)\n- [ ] A new integration test verifies that a state materialized with heater enabled and 10 initial shrimp has `hardware.heater.enabled == true` and `animals.adults == 10`\n\n## Files to Modify/Create\n- `crates/tank_tui/src/main.rs` — Extend `StartupSelection` with new fields (source water, substrate, plants, filter, light, heater, aeration, shrimp count); extend `SelectionField` enum; update `render_startup` to show the new fields and an updated summary panel; update `adjust_left`/`adjust_right` for each new field\n- `crates/tank_scenarios/src/lib.rs` — Add a new `StartupOverrides` struct and a `seeded_state_with_full_overrides` function (or extend `seeded_state_with_overrides`) that accepts hardware settings, initial shrimp count, source water override, substrate override, and plant selection override; apply these after base scenario materialization\n- `crates/tank_core/src/types/biology.rs` — Ensure `AnimalState` can be initialized with a given adult count (may already be possible via field assignment; verify)\n- `crates/tank_scenarios/tests/startup_overrides.rs` — New test: materialize with heater enabled + 10 shrimp, assert `hardware.heater.enabled == true` and `animals.adults == 10`; materialize with different source water, assert water chemistry matches the override profile\n\n## Dependencies\n- Requires: Loop 7 (TUI MVP, Scenario Integration) — completed\n- Blocks: Project completion\n\n---"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7398,"cache_read_input_tokens":38887,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":7398},"output_tokens":10,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"52ade16c-d21b-4a80-87c4-793dd732d7a8","uuid":"d5a409cf-40f0-43ab-8ffb-7ce460384f1e"}
